# Physiology Learning Platform - Local Environment Setup

This document highlights the environment variable configurations required to run and connect both frontend and backend modules outside Docker or locally.

## Spring Boot Backend Environment Variables
```bash
# Database Configuration
SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5433/physiology_db
SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=physiology_user
SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD=physiology_secure_password123

# Caching Configuration
SPRING_DATA_REDIS_HOST=localhost
SPRING_DATA_REDIS_PORT=6379

# Search Engine Configuration
SPRING_ELASTICSEARCH_URIS=http://localhost:9200

# Security Configuration
JWT_SECRET=5367566B59703373367639792F423F4528482B4D6251655468576D5A71347437
JWT_EXPIRATION=86400000 # 24 hours
PORT=8085

# External Integrations
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```

## Next.js Frontend Config
By default, Next.js utilizes port `3000` and redirects `/api/*` traffic automatically to the proxy target at `http://localhost:8085` as configured inside `next.config.js`.
